    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9778\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to\naccept an application for a real property tax exemption from Gurdwara\nGuru Tegh Bahadur Sahib, Inc.\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAuthorizes the County of Nassau to grant a real property tax exemption\nto Gurdwara Guru Tegh Bahadur Sahib, Inc.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the assessor of the county of Nassau to\naccept an application for exemption from real property taxes for the\nproperty owned by Gurdwara Guru Tegh Bahadur Sahib, Inc. If satisfied\nwith such application, the assessor, upon approval by the Nassau County\nLegislature, may make appropriate correction to the subject roll.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would provide Gurdwara Guru Tegh Bahadur Sahib with an\nexemption from real property taxes pursuant to 420-a and 462 of the Real\nProperty Tax Law.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
